{
  // JSDoc + checkJs type baseline (odd/tasks/ts-checkjs-baseline.md).
  //
  // NOTE (deliberate deviation): global checkJs is OFF. With
  // checkJs:true over this include, tsc type-checks EVERY module it can
  // reach at once (~760 errors, ~530 of them in out-of-scope files such as
  // gigs.js, rehearsals.js, services.js, comments.js, bandmates.js,
  // announcements.js, search.js, offlineCache.js, readiness.js, duration.js,
  // chordpro/parser.js). The ODD scopes the baseline to exactly four domain
  // libs, so they opt in individually with the canonical per-file
  // `// @ts-check` pragma — identical checking semantics for the opt-in
  // files, exact checked surface. The remaining modules stay unchecked until
  // a later pass; do NOT flip checkJs on globally before then.
  //
  // PATHS (updated by M0a + jsdoc-libs port): the original opt-in files moved
  // when the tree was relocated into the ADR 0002 boundaries. The old include
  // was ["src/lib"], which now holds only storage.js — tsc exited 0 while
  // checking ONE untyped file, and the whole baseline was silently dead. The
  // globs below are what actually admit the pragma'd files — the four
  // post-M0a baseline files plus the relocated jsdoc-libs pass surface:
  //   src/domain/music/{transpose,annotations}.js
  //   src/data/repositories/{songs,setlists}.js
  //   src/data/repositories/*.js (jsdoc-libs S02-S11 port)
  //   src/domain/** (jsdoc-libs S04-S11 port)
  //   src/integrations/** (jsdoc-libs S05-S08 port)
  //   src/offline/** (jsdoc-libs S09/S11 port)
  //   src/data/supabase.js (jsdoc-libs S11 port — src/data covers it)
  // VERIFY AFTER ANY MOVE: `npx tsc --noEmit --listFiles | grep -c 'cemurm/src/'`
  // must stay > 1. A count of 1 means the baseline is dead again and the
  // green exit is meaningless. 248 at F1: 172 TS/TSX (the template tree) + 76 JS.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    // strict is for the TS/TSX half (tw4-stack-foundation S4). Since F1 the
    // vendored admin template's .ts/.tsx tree is admitted by `include`, and
    // the path aliases below resolve its "@/..." and "src/..." imports.
    // The same flag applies to the pragma'd .js files (checkJs off but
    // @ts-check files are still checked), so the baseline stays the guard:
    // tsc must exit 0 AND the listFiles count below must stay > 1 after any
    // option change.
    "strict": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"],
      "src/*": ["./src/*"]
    },
    "noEmit": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "types": ["vite/client"]
  },
  "include": [
    "src/domain",
    "src/data",
    "src/integrations",
    "src/lib",
    "src/offline",
    "src/api",
    "src/components",
    "src/context",
    "src/hooks",
    "src/layouts",
    "src/routes",
    "src/types",
    "src/views"
  ]
}